{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466514",
      "title": "Modules & Services",
      "lectureOrder": 660,
      "videoOrder": 608,
      "sourceHash": "4b636793cf0523fabbc5bb27505efd56c5131f710acccbfe5b23914af1b7317d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "Instructor: Now that we learned about lazy loading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 6.93,
          "en": "I can finally dive into what's special",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.93,
          "end": 9.96,
          "en": "about Services and Modules, because I mentioned that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.96,
          "end": 12.06,
          "en": "there is something special about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.06,
          "end": 14.91,
          "en": "but I could only explain it after diving into lazy loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.91,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "because it's strongly related to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 21,
          "en": "I want to dive into where you can provide services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21,
          "end": 24.09,
          "en": "and how that affects the instances of the services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.09,
          "end": 25.68,
          "en": "you're working with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.68,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "Now, we can provide services in the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 30.9,
          "en": "We can provide services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.9,
          "end": 33.12,
          "en": "in the AppComponent or other Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.12,
          "end": 35.22,
          "en": "if you remember the services section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.22,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "There, you also could add a provider's key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 39.033,
          "en": "to the component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.96,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "We can also,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 43.83,
          "en": "load services or add services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 47.52,
          "en": "to providers of any Eagerloaded Module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 47.52,
          "end": 50.22,
          "en": "So in the Recipes Module before we added lazy loading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.22,
          "end": 51.54,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.54,
          "end": 54.27,
          "en": "And we're also of course able to add services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.27,
          "end": 57.69,
          "en": "to providers of Lazy-loaded Modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.69,
          "end": 59.64,
          "en": "Of course, we can also provide services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.64,
          "end": 63.72,
          "en": "by adding the provided in root configuration in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.72,
          "end": 67.5,
          "en": "the @injectable decorator, and that would be recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 69.45,
          "en": "for all services that you planned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 72.45,
          "en": "on providing an AppModule otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.45,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "Now, when you provide a service in the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 78.69,
          "en": "or with provided in root in @injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.69,
          "end": 81.69,
          "en": "the services available application wide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 81.69,
          "end": 84.53,
          "en": "and with the service, I also mean the same instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.53,
          "end": 87.33,
          "en": "of that service is available application-wide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.33,
          "end": 90.723,
          "en": "You're always working with the same singleton instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.68,
          "end": 94.97999999999999,
          "en": "If you provide a service in a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.97999999999999,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "no matter if that's the app component or another component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 99.75,
          "en": "then that service is only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.75,
          "end": 103.71000000000001,
          "en": "for dependency injection inside of that component-tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.71000000000001,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "And then all these components will again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 107.37,
          "en": "share the same instance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 110.64,
          "en": "but we're talking only about that component-tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 110.64,
          "end": 112.71000000000001,
          "en": "And if you provide the service in multiple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.71000000000001,
          "end": 114.69,
          "en": "sibling components of your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 114.69,
          "end": 116.85,
          "en": "then all these sibling component trees",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.85,
          "end": 117.99000000000001,
          "en": "have access to the service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 117.99000000000001,
          "end": 119.94,
          "en": "But each component tree has access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 119.94,
          "end": 121.83,
          "en": "to its own service instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 121.83,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "And I mentioned this and showed this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 126.213,
          "en": "in the services margin of this course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 127.59,
          "end": 130.83,
          "en": "Now, the interesting thing is, if you do add a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.83,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "to providers of an Eager-loaded Module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 137.04,
          "en": "you might think that that service is only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 137.04,
          "end": 139.05,
          "en": "inside of that Module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 141.75,
          "en": "and that every Module where you add a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 141.75,
          "end": 144.99,
          "en": "to its providers has its own instance of that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 144.99,
          "end": 147.12,
          "en": "But actually that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.12,
          "end": 149.64,
          "en": "If a Module is Eager-loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 151.71,
          "en": "everything is bundled together initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 151.71,
          "end": 154.62,
          "en": "and therefore any services you add to providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 154.62,
          "end": 156.36,
          "en": "in an Eager-loaded Module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 156.36,
          "end": 159.81,
          "en": "let's say the Recipes Module would be not Lazy-loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 159.81,
          "end": 161.19,
          "en": "but still Eagerly-loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 161.19,
          "end": 163.77,
          "en": "by importing it into the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.77,
          "end": 167.19,
          "en": "Any service added there will be available application-wide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 167.19,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "with one in the same instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "So adding a service to providers of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 171.69,
          "end": 175.68,
          "en": "an Eagerly-loaded Module has the exact same effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 175.68,
          "end": 179.16,
          "en": "as adding a service to providers of the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 179.16,
          "end": 183.81,
          "en": "or as adding provider in root in @injectable has.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 183.81,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "A huge difference can be seen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 188.01,
          "en": "if you add a service to providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 188.01,
          "end": 190.11,
          "en": "of a Lazy-loaded Module though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 190.11,
          "end": 191.91,
          "en": "There the service is only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 191.91,
          "end": 195.33,
          "en": "in that loaded Module and it gets its own instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 198.09,
          "en": "If you do provide a service both in the AppModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 198.09,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "and in the Lazy-loaded Module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 202.8,
          "en": "then the service is of course available application-wide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 202.8,
          "end": 206.01,
          "en": "but the Lazy-loaded Module will get a separate instance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 206.01,
          "end": 208.92000000000002,
          "en": "not the same instance you use in the rest of the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 208.92000000000002,
          "end": 210.93,
          "en": "Sometimes this can be desirable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 210.93,
          "end": 214.02,
          "en": "but in other cases, it might lead to a strange behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 214.02,
          "end": 215.85,
          "en": "where you would've expected to work with one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 218.13,
          "en": "at the same instance when you didn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 218.13,
          "end": 220.8,
          "en": "The reason for that is that when you do provide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 220.8,
          "end": 223.47,
          "en": "in the AppModule or in @injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 223.47,
          "end": 225.72,
          "en": "you use the so-called root injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 225.72,
          "end": 228.933,
          "en": "So the root dependency injection mechanism of angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 229.86,
          "end": 231.57,
          "en": "When you do provide it in a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 233.46,
          "en": "you use the component-specific injector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 233.46,
          "end": 234.84,
          "en": "which is not the root injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 234.84,
          "end": 238.02,
          "en": "and therefore not the entire application has access to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 238.02,
          "end": 239.91,
          "en": "In an Eagerly-loaded Module, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 239.91,
          "end": 242.28,
          "en": "the root injector is used automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 242.28,
          "end": 243.9,
          "en": "With a Lazy-loaded Module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 243.9,
          "end": 247.08,
          "en": "a separate child injector is created by angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 247.08,
          "end": 248.88,
          "en": "for that Module, and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 248.88,
          "end": 252.39,
          "en": "that Module has its own instance of that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 252.39,
          "end": 255.75,
          "en": "Therefore, the default should be that you use the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 255.75,
          "end": 260.4,
          "en": "or again, provided in root in @injectable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 260.4,
          "end": 262.65,
          "en": "You of course might have scenarios where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 262.65,
          "end": 264.99,
          "en": "a component tree needs its own service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 264.99,
          "end": 268.35,
          "en": "For example, if that component tree somehow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 268.35,
          "end": 271.2,
          "en": "has a service that only matters for these components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 271.2,
          "end": 273.03,
          "en": "it doesn't matter application wide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 273.03,
          "end": 274.14,
          "en": "then there is no need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 274.14,
          "end": 275.85,
          "en": "to provide the service application wide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 275.85,
          "end": 278.673,
          "en": "You can instead provide it in that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 280.2,
          "end": 283.2,
          "en": "Eagerly-loaded Modules should pretty much",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 283.2,
          "end": 285.09000000000003,
          "en": "never provide services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 285.09000000000003,
          "end": 287.61,
          "en": "You should avoid this because the effect is the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 287.61,
          "end": 290.49,
          "en": "as in the AppModule, but it's kind of unexpected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 290.49,
          "end": 293.49,
          "en": "and it's harder to detect services there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 293.49,
          "end": 296.58,
          "en": "and therefore other developers diving into your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 296.58,
          "end": 298.59000000000003,
          "en": "might look for a certain service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 298.59000000000003,
          "end": 301.77,
          "en": "might look for it in the AppModule, not find it there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 301.77,
          "end": 303.36,
          "en": "and therefore be confused,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 303.36,
          "end": 306.06,
          "en": "whether this service is now intended to be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 306.06,
          "end": 309.18,
          "en": "to the entire app or only to that Module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 309.18,
          "end": 311.13,
          "en": "Now, in a Lazy-loaded Module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 311.13,
          "end": 313.68,
          "en": "you can of course add a service to providers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 313.68,
          "end": 316.29,
          "en": "but only do this if you deliberately want to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 316.29,
          "end": 318.81,
          "en": "a separate instance of that service there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 318.81,
          "end": 321.15,
          "en": "Otherwise, you can have strange box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 321.15,
          "end": 323.85,
          "en": "So as a rule, generally you wanna ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 323.85,
          "end": 327.24,
          "en": "that services are always available application-wide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 327.24,
          "end": 330.12,
          "en": "by using @injectable provided in root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 330.12,
          "end": 332.90999999999997,
          "en": "or by adding them to providers in the AppModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 332.90999999999997,
          "end": 336.69,
          "en": "unless you have a strong reason for adding them only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 339.57,
          "en": "in a component-tree or in a Lazy-loaded Module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 339.57,
          "end": 343.14,
          "en": "Never add services in an Eager-loaded Module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 343.14,
          "end": 344.74,
          "en": "Now, let's see that in practice.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
